infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title One process vs the fleet: every safety device changes shape
  desc Each per-instance safety device behaves differently at fleet scale — and each needs its own fleet-level fix
  compares
    - label Single process — the intuition
      children
        - label Breaker: one count, one verdict
          desc One process owns the state, so one breaker gives one clean answer
        - label Retries: bounded per call
          desc A retry count caps the calls a single layer makes
        - label Recovery probe: one half-open trickle
          desc A lone breaker sends one probe to test the dependency
        - label Backoff: spreads one client's attempts
          desc Increasing intervals smear a single client's retries over time
        - label Shedding: drops local overload
          desc An instance sheds when its own load runs too high
    - label Across the fleet — the reality
      children
        - label Breaker: 50 counts, no shared view
          desc Fix: accept local fuzziness, or pay for shared state
        - label Retries: multiply 4×4×4 = 64
          desc Fix: retry one layer, cap 60/min per process, breaker above
        - label Recovery probe: 50 breakers herd at once
          desc Fix: jitter the probe timing so probes spread out
        - label Backoff: clients re-sync into waves
          desc Fix: exponential backoff WITH jitter to break correlation
        - label Shedding: shuffles load between instances
          desc Fix: coordinated, priority-based, deadline-aware
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
